{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>צנוף.</b> Derived from מצנפת (Exodus 28:4) — that He will take him along with all his wealth and all his glory." "The kaf of <b>כדור</b> is for comparison, and this locution is well-known from the words of our early Sages of blessed memory, also from the reason of the verse." "<b>ארץ רחבת-ידים.</b> It is Babylonia." "<b>מרכבות כבודך וגו׳.</b> The meaning there is: there he will die, and all your chariots — for you are a disgrace to your master's house; or, it will then be. And the probable view is that this was in the exile of Jehoiakim or Jehoiachin, because of \"and I will call My servant and clothe him with your tunic.\""], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {3 "Ibn Ezra cites the phrase 'וקראתי לעבדי והלבשתיו כתנתך' which corresponds to Isaiah 22:20–21, resolving it as his warrant for dating the event to the exile of Jehoiakim or Jehoiachin."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:44.407025090Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}